# Generated output, not source. exports/ is written by export_bookkeeping.py
# and "Claude outputs/" holds working CSVs from the chart of accounts sessions.
# Both were untracked and both trip config.check_git_status_on_startup()'s
# clean-tree warning before every run, which is the only reason it fires.
exports/
Claude outputs/

# Byte-exact copies taken immediately before an edit, per CLAUDE.md's evidence
# standard. They are proof of a before-state and not source, and git holds the
# real before-state once the edit is committed. Added 2026-09-09 for the reason
# the two lines above give: nine of them were untracked in archive\ and
# config.check_git_status_on_startup() counts untracked files, so every pipeline
# start would have warned "Changed files: 9 file(s)" on a tree that is clean.
*.bak
*.bak-*
